input.prompt:
Your fix works for the reported case, but I found two reachable duplication regressions. Same repo, same file ownership (src/context.ts, src/context.test.ts). Still no git add/commit.

## Problem with current simple append
`#newResponse` (src/context.ts:609-657) builds responses with `new Headers(this.#res.headers)`, so a handler returning `c.text()` / `c.json()` ALREADY carries the middleware's Set-Cookie values. Also `c.res = c.res` self-assignment is reachable (handler returning `c.res` when not finalized). Because your merge now appends every prior cookie unconditionally, both cases duplicate the middleware cookie.

Verified Node behavior: `new Headers(headersWithTwoSetCookies)` preserves both entries, so the duplication is real.

## Required change (src/context.ts setter)
Keep cookies that are already present in the new response from being re-appended. Dedupe by exact value, preserving order (handler/new-response cookies first, then only the prior cookies not already present). Suggested shape:

```ts
set res(_res: Response | undefined) {
  if (this.#res && _res) {
    _res = createResponseInstance(_res.body, _res)
    const cookies = this.#res.headers.getSetCookie()
    for (const [k, v] of this.#res.headers.entries()) {
      if (k === 'content-type' || k === 'set-cookie') {
        continue
      }
      _res.headers.set(k, v)
    }
    if (cookies.length > 0) {
      const present = new Set(_res.headers.getSetCookie())
      for (const cookie of cookies) {
        if (!present.has(cookie)) {
          _res.headers.append('set-cookie', cookie)
        }
      }
    }
  }
  this.#res = _res
  this.finalized = true
}
```

Keep it minimal and in the file's style.

## Tests to add (src/context.test.ts, inside `describe('Context header', ...)`)
Follow TDD: add each test, run it against your current unconditional-append code, record the duplicate failure, then apply the dedupe fix.

1. `Should not duplicate cookies set on c.res when the handler returns c.text()`:
   - `c.res.headers.append('set-cookie', 'session=middleware; Path=/')`
   - `setCookie(c, 'token', 'handler', { path: '/' })` (helper is already imported) OR `const res = c.text('hi')` then assign `c.res = res` — the point is the helper-built response already inherits the cookie.
   - Prefer an app-level test for realism: middleware appends `session=middleware; Path=/` to `c.res.headers`, handler returns `c.text('hi')`; assert `res.headers.getSetCookie()` equals `['session=middleware; Path=/']` exactly (no duplicates).
2. `Should not duplicate cookies when assigning c.res to itself`:
   - `c.res.headers.append('set-cookie', 'a=1')`; `c.res = c.res`; assert `c.res.headers.getSetCookie()` equals `['a=1']`.

Keep the existing new regression test (handler-set cookie + middleware cookie both survive, exact 2-element array) and the updated reassignment test unchanged.

## Verification (required)
- `pnpm exec vp test --run src/context.test.ts` — all green.
- `pnpm exec vp test --run --project main src/hono.test.ts src/middleware/csrf src/helper/cookie` — all green.
- `pnpm exec tsc -p tsconfig.spec.json --noEmit` — exit 0.

## Report back
- Final `git diff -- src/context.ts src/context.test.ts`.
- The pre-fix duplicate failure output for both new tests.
- Test summary counts and tsc result.

